{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Refresh IRIS Index",
  "description": "Manually refresh the IRIS index for this repo — the codebase index, plus the project artifact index when an artifact directory is configured. Deliberately manual: reindexing calls AWS Bedrock per changed file and summaries of half-finished code are worse than slightly stale ones. The iris-query skill detects staleness on every question, so run this when you have reached a good stopping point.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "userTriggered"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Refresh the IRIS index for this repo using the iris-query skill (Task 3). Run scripts/iris_setup_lite.sh against the current repo root. It refreshes the codebase index, and also the artifact index when .iris_cache/iris_skill_config.yaml records an artifact_dir. Indexing is incremental, so report per index whether it was a no-op or which files/artifacts were reprocessed. If the iris package or AWS credentials are missing, report exactly what is missing and stop — do not attempt to install anything. If an artifact index exists but its artifact_dir is not reachable on this machine, say so instead of silently refreshing the codebase only."
  }
}
